  | No Auth Access | POST /api/posts without token | Rejected with 401 | ✅ Mitigated |
  | Token Reuse After Logout | Using logged-out token | Rejected with 401 | ✅ Mitigated |
  | Empty Body Registration | POST /api/register with {} | Rejected with 422 | ✅ Mitigated |
  ## 6. RESOURCE CLEANUP
  - [x] 'docker compose down' executed successfully.
  ## 7. FINAL SIGN-OFF
  **Justification**: 21 of 22 tests passed (95.45% pass rate). However, QA-11 constitutes a **SPEC VIOLATION**: the technical
  specification clearly states a maximum page size of 50 (`max size 50` in §3.1), but the backend accepts values up to at least 100
  without validation. This is a contractual breach between the implementation and the documented specification. Additionally, the XSS
  payload was stored successfully without sanitization at the API layer, relying entirely on frontend escaping. While architectural
  choices may justify this, it remains a risk. The spec violation is the primary rejection reason.
