  Output: # Code Review Report — LiteChat V1 (MVP)
  ## Scope Audit Summary
  - **Review Type**: Red-team security & scope alignment audit
  - **Auditor**: Principal Software Architect & Security Auditor
  - **Target**: LiteChat V1 MVP — backend (Python/FastAPI) + frontend (Vanilla JS/Nginx)
  - **Reference Documents**: `boundary_manifest.md`, `requirements.md`
  ---
  ## 1. Scope Alignment Audit
  ### 1.1 Media Processing (Uploads, Avatar, CDN)
  - **Banned entities checked**: `UploadFile`, `FileUpload`, `FileStorage`, `OSS`, `S3`, `CDN`, `Avatar`,
  `ImageField`, `MediaFile`, `FileField`
  - **Banned routes checked**: `/upload`, `/media`, `/file`
  - **Banned DB fields checked**: `avatar_url`, `image_path`, `file_attachment`
  - **Actual implementation**: No file upload endpoints exist. No media-related imports or classes. Database schema
  contains no media-related columns. Requirements.txt has no media-related libraries.
  - **Verdict: ✅ CLEAN**
  ### 1.2 Social Interaction Beyond Likes (Comment, Reply, DM, Follow, Share)
  - **Banned entities checked**: `Comment`, `Reply`, `PrivateMessage`, `DM`, `DirectMessage`, `Friendship`,
  `Follow`, `Unfollow`, `Following`, `Follower`, `Share`, `Message`
  - **Banned routes checked**: `/comment`, `/reply`, `/message`, `/dm`, `/follow`, `/unfollow`, `/share`
  - **Banned DB tables checked**: `comments`, `messages`, `friendships`, `followers`
  - **Actual implementation**: No comment, message, follow, or share functionality exists. Only `likes` table
  (explicitly permitted) handles social interaction. All API routes are limited to `/api/posts/{id}/like` for
  like/unlike operations.
  - **Verdict: ✅ CLEAN**
  ### 1.3 Recommendation Algorithm / ML
  - **Banned entities checked**: `RecommendationModel`, `MLModel`, `UserProfile`, `UserTaste`,
  `CollaborativeFiltering`, `ContentFeatureExtraction`, `Recommender`, `UserEmbedding`
  - **Banned dependencies checked**: `scikit-learn`, `numpy` (ML usage), `tensorflow`, `pytorch`
  - **Actual implementation**: The feed sorting uses a simple bubble-up heat-weighting rule (`>=5 likes
  difference`), which is explicitly in scope per requirements.md Rule 3. No ML models, user profiling, or
  collaborative filtering present. Dependencies are only `fastapi`, `uvicorn`, `bcrypt`, `python-multipart`.
  - **Verdict: ✅ CLEAN**
  ### 1.4 Advanced Authentication (OAuth, Email/SMS, Password Reset)
  - **Banned entities checked**: `GoogleOAuth`, `GitHubOAuth`, `WeChatOAuth`, `OAuthLogin`, `EmailVerification`,
  `SMSVerification`, `SMSCode`, `ResetPassword`, `ForgotPassword`, `PasswordReset`, `EmailField`, `PhoneField`
  - **Banned routes checked**: `/auth/google`, `/auth/github`, `/reset-password`, `/forgot-password`,
  `/verify-email`, `/sms`
  - **Actual implementation**: Authentication is strictly username+password with bcrypt hashing (cost 12). No OAuth,
  email, SMS, or password reset functionality. No email/phone fields in the users table. Session token-based auth
  using 32-byte hex tokens.
  - **Verdict: ✅ CLEAN**

  ### 1.5 Scope Requirements Coverage (Positive Check)
  | Requirement ID | Feature | Status | Evidence |
  |:---|:---|---:|:---|
  | FR-01 | User Registration (username+password, bcrypt, unique) | ✅ | `/api/register`, `hash_password()` with
  bcrypt cost 12, UNIQUE constraint on username |
  | FR-02 | User Login (password verify, session/token) | ✅ | `/api/login`, `verify_password()`, `create_session()`
  with 24h expiry |
  | FR-03 | Post Text Content (<500 chars, no media) | ✅ | `/api/posts` POST, `max_length=500`, `html.escape()` for
  XSS, no file fields |
  | FR-04 | Browse Feed (time desc + heat-weighted) | ✅ | `/api/posts` GET, bubble-sort for >=5 like difference |
  | FR-05 | Like/Unlike (unique per user per post) | ✅ | `/api/posts/{id}/like` POST/DELETE, UNIQUE(user_id,
  post_id) constraint |
  | FR-06 | Logout (session clear) | ✅ | `/api/logout`, `delete_session()` |
  | Rule 1 | <500 chars per post | ✅ | `max_length=500` in Pydantic model, frontend char count |
  | Rule 2 | Like uniqueness (one per user per post) | ✅ | UNIQUE constraint + duplicate check in like_post |
  | Rule 3 | Simple heat-weighted sorting (no ML) | ✅ | Bubble-up sort on >=5 like difference |
  | Rule 4 | Username: alphanumeric+underscore, 3-20 chars | ✅ | Regex `^[a-zA-Z0-9_]{3,20}$` |
  | Rule 5 | Password >=6 chars, bcrypt hashed | ✅ | `min_length=6`, `bcrypt.hashpw()` with cost 12 |
  | NFR | XSS protection | ✅ | `html.escape()` on backend, `textContent` / custom `escapeHtml()` on frontend |
  | NFR | Rate limiting | ✅ | 10/min register/login per IP, 30 posts/hour per user, 60 likes/min per user |
  ---
  ## 2. Actionable Feedback
  **No violations found.** The codebase is fully compliant with both `boundary_manifest.md` and `requirements.md`.
  All implemented features are within the defined scope. No banned functional entities, API endpoints, database
  tables, or dependencies were detected.
  The implementation:
  - Correctly avoids all file upload/media handling (no UploadFile, no Avatar, no image fields)
  - Correctly limits social interaction to likes only (no comments, DMs, follows, shares)
  - Correctly uses simple rule-based sorting instead of ML algorithms
  - Correctly implements basic username+password auth without OAuth, email, SMS, or password reset
  - Correctly implements all P0 features (register, login, posts, feed, likes, logout)
  No changes required.
  ---
  ## Review Verdict: APPROVED

