  Output: # Tech Specs — LiteChat V1
  ## 1. Architecture Overview
  ### 1.1 Two-Container Strategy
  - **Backend Container**: Python FastAPI server (port 8000) — serves REST API, owns SQLite database, handles auth,
  posts, and likes.
  - **Frontend Container**: Nginx (port 80) — serves static HTML/JS/CSS assets, proxies API calls to backend.
  - **Orchestration**: docker-compose.yml with healthcheck on backend and `condition: service_healthy` on frontend
  depends_on.
  ### 1.2 Tech Stack
  | Layer | Technology | Version |
  |:---|:---|:---|
  | Backend Runtime | Python | 3.11-slim |
  | Web Framework | FastAPI | 0.104+ |
  | ASGI Server | Uvicorn | 0.24+ |
  | Database | SQLite3 | Built-in |
  | Password Hashing | bcrypt | 4.1+ |
  | Frontend Server | Nginx | 1.25-alpine |
  | Frontend UI | Vanilla HTML/CSS/JS | — |
  | Container Runtime | Docker Compose | V2+ |
  ## 2. API Endpoints
  ### 2.1 Auth Routes
  | Method | Path | Auth | Description |
  |:---|:---|:---|:---|
  | POST | /api/register | No | Register new user (username + password) |
  | POST | /api/login | No | Login, returns session token |
  | POST | /api/logout | Yes | Logout, destroys session |
  ### 2.2 Post Routes
  | Method | Path | Auth | Description |
  |:---|:---|:---|:---|
  | GET | /api/posts | No | List all posts (sorted by time + heat) |
  | POST | /api/posts | Yes | Create a new text post (< 500 chars) |
  ### 2.3 Like Routes
  | Method | Path | Auth | Description |
  |:---|:---|:---|:---|
  | POST | /api/posts/{id}/like | Yes | Like a post |
  | DELETE | /api/posts/{id}/like | Yes | Unlike a post |
  ## 3. Database Schema (SQLite)
  ### 3.1 users table
  ```sql
  CREATE TABLE users (
      id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
      username TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL,
      password_hash TEXT NOT NULL,
      created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
  );
  ```
  ### 3.2 posts table
  ```sql
  CREATE TABLE posts (
      id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
      user_id INTEGER NOT NULL,
      content TEXT NOT NULL,
      created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
      FOREIGN KEY (user_id) REFERENCES users(id)
  );
  ```
  ### 3.3 likes table
  ```sql
  CREATE TABLE likes (
      id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
      user_id INTEGER NOT NULL,
      post_id INTEGER NOT NULL,
      created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
      FOREIGN KEY (user_id) REFERENCES users(id),
      FOREIGN KEY (post_id) REFERENCES posts(id),
      UNIQUE(user_id, post_id)
  );
  ```
  ## 4. Business Logic Rules
  ### 4.1 Content Sorting (Rule 3)
  - Default sort: `created_at DESC`
  - Heat weighting: If a post has >= 5 more likes than the post above it, swap positions (simple bubble-up).
  - Threshold check performed at query time only (no background job).
  ### 4.2 Rate Limiting
  - Login/Register: max 10 attempts per IP per minute (in-memory sliding window).
  - Post creation: max 30 posts per user per hour.
  - Like operations: max 60 per user per minute.
  ### 4.3 Input Validation
  - Username: 3-20 chars, alphanumeric + underscore only (`^[a-zA-Z0-9_]{3,20}$`).
  - Password: min 6 chars, no other constraints.
  - Post content: max 500 chars, HTML-escaped before storage/display.
  ## 5. Security Measures
  - Passwords hashed with bcrypt (cost factor 12).
  - Session tokens are 32-byte hex strings from `secrets.token_hex(32)`.
  - All user output HTML-escaped via Python `html.escape()`.
  - CORS enabled only for frontend origin.
  ## 6. Healthcheck Configuration
  - Backend healthcheck: `curl -f http://localhost:8000/health || exit 1`
    - Interval: 30s, Timeout: 10s, Retries: 3, Start period: 10s
